---

<div class="space-y-12 text-surface-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
  <!-- Section 1 -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-surface-950 tracking-tight">
      Optimizing images for social media platforms
    </h2>
    <p>
      Every major social network enforces distinct display aspect ratios, target resolutions, and automated compression algorithms. Uploading an improperly sized photograph often triggers aggressive automated cropping or algorithmic blurriness that cuts off focal subjects, distorts text graphics, and degrades visual branding.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/80 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-surface-900 text-sm flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-rose-500"></span>
          Instagram & Threads
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
          Standardizes on vertical Portrait (4:5, 1080×1350) for maximum screen presence in mobile feeds, Square (1:1, 1080×1080) for grid posts, and full-screen vertical Stories & Reels (9:16, 1080×1920).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/80 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-surface-900 text-sm flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-blue-600"></span>
          LinkedIn & X / Twitter
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
          Optimizes for widescreen Landscape (1.91:1 and 16:9, 1200×630 / 1200×675) for in-stream link previews and company announcements, alongside wide banner headers (3:1 and 4:1) for profile pages.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/80 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-surface-900 text-sm flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-red-600"></span>
          YouTube, TikTok & Pinterest
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
          YouTube demands high-definition 16:9 thumbnails (1280×720), Pinterest thrives on 2:3 vertical standard pins (1000×1500), and TikTok relies strictly on 9:16 vertical video covers (1080×1920).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2 -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-surface-950 tracking-tight">
      Crop to Fill vs. Fit Entire Image explained
    </h2>
    <p>
      When your source image does not share the exact aspect ratio of the social media preset, you have two fundamental framing options:
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/80 space-y-2">
        <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md bg-brand-100 text-brand-800 font-bold text-xs">Recommended for Feeds</span>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-surface-900">Crop to Fill (No Distortion)</h3>
        <p class="text-surface-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
          Scales your photograph proportionally until it completely covers the target width and height. Pixels that spill outside the boundaries are trimmed away according to your chosen 3x3 focal position. This guarantees zero black bars, no letterboxing, and no unnatural stretching.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/80 space-y-2">
        <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md bg-surface-200 text-surface-800 font-bold text-xs">For Complete Graphics & Art</span>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-surface-900">Fit Entire Image (Letterbox / Pillarbox)</h3>
        <p class="text-surface-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
          Scales your photograph so that 100% of the original content fits comfortably inside the preset dimensions without discarding any pixels. Any extra space is padded with a clean solid white backdrop (or transparent canvas for PNG and WebP), preserving full logos, documents, and product banners.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3 -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-surface-950 tracking-tight">
      Mastering the 3x3 focal alignment grid
    </h2>
    <p>
      Automated center-cropping often cuts off heads in vertical portraits or clips off-center subjects in landscape compositions. Our interactive 3x3 focal alignment grid gives you complete directorial control:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-surface-600">
      <li>
        <strong>Top / Top-Center:</strong> Essential for human portraits, headshots, and fashion photography to ensure faces and hats are never chopped off when converting to landscape or square formats.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Center:</strong> Ideal for balanced product photos, centered logos, symmetrical architecture, and abstract textures.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Left / Right:</strong> Perfect for environmental portraits or rule-of-thirds compositions where the primary subject is framed along the side of the viewfinder.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bottom / Corners:</strong> Recommended for landscape vistas where foreground flowers, reflections, or water shorelines constitute the critical visual anchor.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4 -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
